    //- ── Config Snippet Library ─────────────
    .help-section
      button.help-section-title(type='button', (click)='toggleHelpSection("snippets")')
        span.help-chevron {{ isSectionOpen('snippets') ? '▾' : '▸' }}
        | Config Snippet Library
      .help-section-body(*ngIf='isSectionOpen("snippets")')
        p
          strong Overview:
          |  Save and reuse reusable configuration fragments. Snippets support variable interpolation — any
          |
          span.help-code {{ '{{' }}variable{{ '}}' }}
          |  placeholder is automatically replaced with the selected node's properties when inserted.
        p
          strong Accessing snippets:
          |  Select a node → Config tab → click
          |
          span.help-tag Snippets
          |  button at the bottom of the config actions bar.
        p
          strong Snippet panel features:
        ul
          li
            span.help-tag Category filter
            |  — filter by: interface, routing, security, qos, system, other
          li
            span.help-tag Search
            |  — free-text search across snippet names and content
          li
            span.help-tag Insert
            |  — click a snippet to insert it at the cursor position (or append to config)
          li
            span.help-tag Save
            |  — save the current config as a new named snippet with a category
          li
            span.help-tag Delete
            |  — remove a snippet from the library
        p
          strong Variable interpolation:
          |  When inserting a snippet, these placeholders are replaced automatically:
        table.help-table
          thead: tr
            th Placeholder
            th Replaced With
          tbody
            tr
              td: span.help-code {{ '{{' }}hostname{{ '}}' }}
              td Node label
            tr
              td: span.help-code {{ '{{' }}mgmt_ip{{ '}}' }}
              td Management IP (without CIDR)
            tr
              td: span.help-code {{ '{{' }}vendor{{ '}}' }}
              td Vendor name
            tr
              td: span.help-code {{ '{{' }}model{{ '}}' }}
              td Device model
            tr
              td: span.help-code {{ '{{' }}asn{{ '}}' }}
              td BGP ASN
            tr
              td: span.help-code {{ '{{' }}loopback{{ '}}' }}
              td Loopback IP
        p
          strong Storage:
          |  Snippets are stored in
          |
          span.help-code netops-snippets.json
          |  inside the Electron userData directory. They persist across sessions and topologies.

    //- ── Workspaces, Export & Import ───────
    .help-section
      button.help-section-title(type='button', (click)='toggleHelpSection("workspace")')
        span.help-chevron {{ isSectionOpen('workspace') ? '▾' : '▸' }}
        | Workspaces, Export & Import
      .help-section-body(*ngIf='isSectionOpen("workspace")')
        p
          strong Tabs:
          |  Each tab is an independent topology with its own inventory. Click "+" to add a tab. Double-click a tab to rename it. A "•" dot appears on tabs with unsaved changes. Middle-click a tab to close it. Right-click tab → Open in New Window.
        p
          strong Save Workspace
          |  (
          span.help-kbd Ctrl+Shift+S
          | ): All tabs →
          |
          span.help-code .workspace.json
          | . Open Workspace (File menu) restores the full session.
        p
          strong File formats:
          |
          span.help-code .topo.json
          |  (topology) ·
          span.help-code .inv.json
          |  (inventory sidecar) ·
          span.help-code .workspace.json
          |  (multi-tab)
        p
          strong Exports:
        ul
          li
            span.help-tag Ansible Inventory
            |  — YAML hosts file
          li
            span.help-tag GNS3 Project
            |  — .gns3 archive
          li
            span.help-tag Containerlab Topology
            |  — .clab.yml for SONiC-VS / multi-vendor virtual lab (export file or deploy directly)
          li
            span.help-tag IP Matrix CSV
            |  — Node / Port / IP (re-importable)
          li
            span.help-tag HTML Report
            |  — Standalone with SVG diagram
          li
            span.help-tag Download All Configs
            |  — All startup configs
          li
            span.help-tag Inventory JSON / Alarms CSV
            |  — State and alarm exports
          li
            span.help-tag Device CSV
            |  — Export from Devices menu
        p
          strong Imports:
          |  IP Matrix CSV (Export menu) · Device CSV (Devices menu) · Drag-and-drop
          |
          span.help-code .json
          |  files onto canvas.
